{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/763058-feedback-needed-questions-about-classic-met-books","id":763058,"title":"(Feedback Needed) Questions About Classic MET Books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-11T06:33:14-08:00","id":763058,"title":"(Feedback Needed) Questions About Classic MET Books","content":"Okay, I am thinking of buying hard copies of old MET books off of Amazon and I have some questions so I know what I am looking for. Please do not recommend By Night Studio's LARP rules, I have no interest in BNS's products for various reasons, the biggest reason being that old copies of WW's MET books are usually cheaper and I am already familiar with those rules anyway.<br /> <br /> I am familiar with Laws of the Night Revised (it's what my old LARP group used) and it's okay although metaplot-heavy, and I own a hard copy of MET The Masquerade 1st Edition which is not what I am looking for. I am interested in Laws of the Night 2e (the gray Laws of the Night book, not the green Revised one), but I need to know what all is in it. Most importantly, are all 13 core clans and their Disciplines in that particular edition of Laws of the Night? I know they're all in Laws of the Night Revised, but there are some issues I have with Revised, namely that the Gangrel are listed as Independent and the Week of Nightmares is mentioned in the section on the Ravnos. While I always Rule Zero the metaplot out of existence, I intend to ST a small LARP in the near future and I don't want to have the headache of explaining the metaplot to new players and then explain that I am not going to use it. But that aside, what all is in Laws of the Night 2e? I have heard it is smaller than Revised and doesn't contain as much background fluff, but does it have all I need for a base game (all 13 clans and their Disciplines as well as the base mechanics)?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what about Laws of the Wild? Which one should I get? Laws of the Night 2e or Revised? Does Revised include rules for playing Stargazers? What supplement books should I get for either Laws of the Night or Laws of the Wild?<br /> <br /> Finally, there's Laws of the Ascension. For some strange reason, Mage did not get a MET version until Revised Edition, and of all the games that got altered the most by metaplot, Mage takes the cake. But that's not too important, what is important is how much does the Avatar Storm factor into the mechanics of MET Mage? Is it easy to handwave? (even if it isn't, I can still find a way to make it work)<br /> <br /> Essentially, these are the MET books I seek to get for my collection. I need to know the pros, cons, and things to know about these books<br /> <br /> <b>Laws of the Night </b>(either 2e or Revised)<br /> <b>Laws of the Wild<br /> Laws of the Ascension<br /> Laws of the Hunt Revised<br /> Laws of the East</b><br /> <br /> Now, are these books worth getting as well? For me, these books aren't first-run must haves, but I do seek to acquire them for later.<br /> <br /> <b>The Shining Host<br /> Laws of the Reckoning<br /> Oblivion</b><br /> <br /> Now, are there any supplements worth acquiring such as Laws of the Elysium, Player Guides, or anything else I need to know about? Any help and information is appreciated greatly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T18:36:49-08:00","id":763649,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> Laws of the Night Revised would be better IMO. Laws 1st has all of the Clans and Disciplines, but uses some slightly clunky mechanics (their version of Beast Traits isn't great) and doesn't have all the powers (powers have 1 Basic/2 Intermediate/1 Advanced, rather than 5 total like Revised).<br /> <br /> The players guides and Laws of Elysium are useful if you're going to be focusing on those portions of the games and sects. They go in depth about how to play the Camarilla, the Sabbat, the Anarchs -- with setting information and metaplot and other specifics, as well as powers and abilities, extra Ability traits and such, that go with those sects. Laws of Elysium, as well as parts of the Camarilla Guide, go into depth about playing Elders, so if you're going to have Elders or lots of heavy Social stuff, Elysium might be useful.<br /> <br /> The Shining Host is pretty good, if you like Dreaming. The system for Bunks is serviceable and roughly thematic, if a little weird in mechanical execution.<br /> <br /> The Avatar Storm factors into Laws of the Ascension Revised when mages cross the Gauntlet or reach across to do magic. It's easily excised. Do note that if you want playable Technocrats, you need the Laws of the Ascension Player's Guide; the core only covers the Traditions.<br /> <br /> I don't like Apocalypse so I can't give you any real input on Wild, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","user":"thebiglarpnerd","date":". 11-11-2015, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T03:45:12-08:00","id":763924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/763058-feedback-needed-questions-about-classic-met-books?p=763649#post763649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> Laws of the Night Revised would be better IMO. Laws 1st has all of the Clans and Disciplines, but uses some slightly clunky mechanics (their version of Beast Traits isn't great) and doesn't have all the powers (powers have 1 Basic/2 Intermediate/1 Advanced, rather than 5 total like Revised).<br /> <br /> The players guides and Laws of Elysium are useful if you're going to be focusing on those portions of the games and sects. They go in depth about how to play the Camarilla, the Sabbat, the Anarchs -- with setting information and metaplot and other specifics, as well as powers and abilities, extra Ability traits and such, that go with those sects. Laws of Elysium, as well as parts of the Camarilla Guide, go into depth about playing Elders, so if you're going to have Elders or lots of heavy Social stuff, Elysium might be useful.<br /> <br /> The Shining Host is pretty good, if you like Dreaming. The system for Bunks is serviceable and roughly thematic, if a little weird in mechanical execution.<br /> <br /> The Avatar Storm factors into Laws of the Ascension Revised when mages cross the Gauntlet or reach across to do magic. It's easily excised. Do note that if you want playable Technocrats, you need the Laws of the Ascension Player's Guide; the core only covers the Traditions.<br /> <br /> I don't like Apocalypse so I can't give you any real input on Wild, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your input, I will probably get Revised and just excise the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}